# 100 Mechanical CAD Generation Test Prompts

**Purpose:** Benchmark a text-to-CAD workstation from basic geometry to advanced, multi-part mechanical assemblies.

## How to run this benchmark

- Run each prompt independently. Do not send multiple prompts in one request.
- Use millimetres (mm) unless a prompt explicitly specifies otherwise.
- Unless the system supports a different intended workflow, request separate editable components for assemblies and a STEP export for the final result.
- For every result, record: whether code/geometry generated; solid count; bounding dimensions; dimensional accuracy; feature correctness; assembly alignment; collisions/clearances; STEP export and re-import; retries; and generation time.
- Do not award a pass merely because a model renders. Check the stated geometry and assembly requirements. Treat a motion or stress requirement as unverified unless the system actually performs the relevant analysis.
- Standards-based items use nominal geometry for CAD testing. Do not assume a generated model is certified for manufacture or safety-critical use.

