# Level 1 — Easy (20 prompts)

### E01 — Cylindrical spacer sleeve
Create one cylindrical spacer sleeve, 30 mm long, with an outside diameter of 24 mm and a through-bore of 12 mm. Keep both end faces flat and parallel, and add a 0.5 mm × 45° chamfer to every circular edge. Produce one valid solid with a continuous open bore, not a filled cylinder or separate inner and outer solids. Export a STEP file.

### E02 — Stepped shaft
Create a stepped shaft with a total length of 100 mm. From the left end, use a Ø20 mm section 25 mm long, a Ø30 mm shoulder section 35 mm long, and a Ø16 mm end section 40 mm long. Keep the three sections coaxial and make the shoulders square. Add 1 mm × 45° chamfers only to the two outer end edges; preserve the shoulder edges.

### E03 — Rectangular mounting plate
Model a 120 × 80 × 8 mm rectangular plate. Add four Ø9 mm through-holes, with hole centres 12 mm from each adjacent edge. The hole pattern must be symmetric about both plate centre lines. Keep the top and bottom faces planar and create exactly one solid.

### E04 — L-shaped angle bracket
Create an L-bracket from two perpendicular plates, each 60 mm long and 50 mm high/wide as appropriate, with 6 mm wall thickness and a 50 mm common width. Unite the plates into one connected solid. Add two Ø8 mm through-holes on each leg, centred across the 50 mm width and spaced 30 mm apart. Do not leave an internal gap at the corner.

### E05 — Circular flange disc
Create a circular flange 100 mm in outside diameter and 10 mm thick with a Ø30 mm central through-bore. Add six Ø8 mm through-holes on a 70 mm pitch-circle diameter, equally spaced at 60° intervals. Centre the hole pattern on the flange and keep all holes open through the thickness.

### E06 — Solid cylindrical roller
Create a solid roller 60 mm long and Ø40 mm in diameter. Add a 2 mm-wide × 1 mm-deep circumferential groove centred along the length. Break both end perimeter edges with a 1 mm × 45° chamfer. The groove must not cut through the roller or split it into multiple bodies.

### E07 — Rectangular block with a blind pocket
Model a 70 × 50 × 25 mm solid block. Cut a centred rectangular pocket measuring 30 × 20 mm and 12 mm deep into the top face. Keep a flat pocket floor and uniform 20 mm margins to the two 30 mm-long side ends, as applicable from the centred placement. The pocket must be subtractive and the result must remain one solid.

### E08 — Hexagonal nut blank
Create a regular hexagonal prism 13 mm across flats and 8 mm thick, with a centred Ø6.8 mm through-bore. Add a 0.5 mm × 45° chamfer to the six outside top and bottom edges and a 0.4 mm × 45° chamfer to both bore entrances. Model nominal CAD geometry only; a helical thread is not required.

### E09 — Pin with retaining groove
Create a straight pin Ø10 mm and 55 mm long. Add a circumferential retaining groove 1.5 mm wide and 0.8 mm deep, positioned 8 mm from one end. Apply a 0.5 mm × 45° chamfer to both end edges. Preserve a cylindrical main body and one groove at the specified axial location.

### E10 — U-channel section
Create a straight U-channel 100 mm long, 40 mm wide, 30 mm tall, and 3 mm thick. The bottom web and two side walls must form one connected solid with a constant wall thickness. Keep the channel open along its entire length and do not accidentally close either end.

### E11 — Hollow pipe segment
Create a straight pipe 120 mm long, with Ø32 mm outside diameter and Ø24 mm inside diameter. Both openings must pass completely through the part. Add an external 2 mm-wide circumferential groove centred 20 mm from one end, with a radial depth of 1 mm. Preserve at least 2 mm wall thickness everywhere.

### E12 — Circular cover plate
Model a Ø90 mm circular cover plate, 6 mm thick, with a Ø20 mm centre hole and four Ø6 mm mounting holes on a 70 mm pitch circle. Add a shallow annular recess on the top face, from Ø38 mm to Ø50 mm, 1.5 mm deep. Keep the centre hole open and produce one solid.

### E13 — Rectangular mounting boss
Create a 60 × 40 × 12 mm base plate with a centred cylindrical boss Ø24 mm and 15 mm high on its top face. Add a Ø10 mm vertical through-hole through both the boss and base. Add four Ø6 mm mounting holes in the plate, each centre 8 mm from the nearest corner. Unite the boss and plate into one solid.

### E14 — Clevis lug
Create a clevis-style lug with a 30 × 20 × 8 mm base and two parallel ears, each 20 mm tall, 8 mm thick, and 20 mm wide, separated by a 12 mm clear gap. Each ear has a coaxial Ø8 mm transverse hole whose centre is 12 mm above the base top. The ears and base must form one connected component; the two holes must align exactly.

### E15 — Triangular gusset bracket
Create a right-triangular gusset plate 6 mm thick with 60 mm horizontal and vertical legs. Attach it to a 60 × 40 × 6 mm L-shaped base-and-wall bracket so the gusset reinforces the inside corner. Add two Ø6 mm mounting holes in the base and two in the upright wall. Unite the gusset and bracket into one solid.

### E16 — Square enclosure lid
Create a 100 × 100 × 5 mm square lid with four Ø5.5 mm corner mounting holes, each centre 8 mm from both adjacent edges. Add a raised central rectangular pad 40 × 30 × 2 mm. Keep the pad centred and the lid underside flat.

### E17 — Spherical-ended handle knob
Create a handle knob comprising a Ø32 mm spherical outer head joined to a Ø12 mm cylindrical stem 25 mm long. Include a centred M8 nominal mounting bore 12 mm deep from the bottom of the stem, represented as a Ø6.8 mm pilot hole if helical threads are unsupported. Ensure the sphere and stem overlap sufficiently to form one solid.

### E18 — Cable gland body
Create a cable gland body with a hexagonal wrench section 24 mm across flats and 10 mm long, a front cylindrical nose Ø18 mm × 12 mm, and a rear threaded-interface cylinder Ø20 mm × 12 mm. Cut a centred Ø10 mm cable passage through the entire part. Represent external threads by a smooth nominal cylinder; keep the passage continuous.

### E19 — Simple finned heat sink
Create an aluminium-style heat-sink geometry with a 100 × 60 × 6 mm base and eight parallel fins. Each fin is 2 mm thick, 35 mm tall above the base, and 60 mm long; space the fins evenly across the 100 mm base width with equal side margins. Join all fins to the base as one solid and keep the channels open along the fin length.

### E20 — Cylindrical knob with radial holes
Create a Ø40 mm × 25 mm cylindrical knob with a Ø8 mm axial bore. Add two Ø4 mm radial holes at 90° around the circumference, each intersecting the axial bore and centred 12.5 mm from the bottom face. Add 1 mm × 45° chamfers to the outer top and bottom circular edges only.

