# Level 2 — Medium (30 prompts)

### M01 — Pillow-block bearing housing
Create a single-piece pillow-block housing with a 120 × 50 × 12 mm mounting base and a raised bearing pedestal 50 mm wide. Place a centred Ø52 mm bearing seat through the pedestal, with the bore axis parallel to the base length direction. Add two Ø12 mm mounting slots, each 24 mm long overall, centred 80 mm apart along the base. Include 6 mm fillets at the pedestal-to-base junction and retain adequate material around the bearing seat.

### M02 — Flanged straight pipe connector
Create a 150 mm-long hollow connector with pipe OD 40 mm and ID 30 mm. Add a 12 mm-thick flange, Ø80 mm OD, at each end; keep both flange faces perpendicular to the pipe axis. Each flange has four Ø9 mm through-holes on an Ø60 mm pitch circle. Fuse the flanges to the pipe and retain a continuous Ø30 mm flow passage.

### M03 — 90-degree hollow pipe elbow
Model a 90° elbow with a constant Ø32 mm outside diameter and Ø24 mm inside diameter along a centreline bend radius of 48 mm. Provide 25 mm straight tangents at both ends. Add circular end collars of Ø44 mm OD and 8 mm axial thickness, each with two Ø6 mm bolt holes on a Ø34 mm pitch circle. Ensure the inner passage follows the bend and has no blocked openings or invalid self-intersections.

### M04 — Machinist V-block
Create a 100 × 50 × 40 mm V-block. Cut a 90° V-groove along the full 100 mm length, centred across the 50 mm width, with the groove apex 10 mm above the bottom face. Add two Ø10 mm vertical mounting holes through the base, 70 mm apart and symmetrically placed. Add a shallow 2 mm-deep × 8 mm-wide relief groove around the top edges only if it does not break the V surfaces.

### M05 — Adjustable slotted mounting bracket
Create a 100 × 60 × 8 mm base with an upright plate 60 mm wide, 45 mm tall, and 8 mm thick at one short edge. Add two horizontal slots 24 × 9 mm in the base and two vertical slots 20 × 9 mm in the upright. Slot ends must be semicircular, dimensions refer to overall slot length and width, and the bracket must be one connected solid with a 6 mm internal corner fillet.

### M06 — Spur gear with hub
Generate a 24-tooth external spur gear using module 2 mm and a 20° pressure angle, with a 12 mm face width and Ø12 mm through-bore. Provide a centred hub Ø30 mm OD × 8 mm long on one side and a 1 mm keyway in the bore is not required; instead cut a 4 mm-wide × 2 mm-deep keyway into the bore wall. Use an actual or well-documented approximate involute tooth profile, maintain circular pitch consistency, and avoid intersecting or disconnected teeth.

### M07 — Single-start worm and wheel test pair
Create a simplified gear-pair assembly consisting of a single-start worm and a 20-tooth worm wheel with module 2 mm nominal sizing. The worm axis and wheel axis must be perpendicular and offset for plausible meshing. Include a Ø12 mm worm shaft with 35 mm usable length and a wheel hub with Ø10 mm bore. This is a geometry/placement test; label mesh geometry as approximate unless a true worm-gear profile is implemented, and do not claim validated transmission behaviour.

### M08 — Bearing end cap
Create a circular end cap Ø100 mm and 12 mm thick with a central Ø40 mm counterbore 5 mm deep and a Ø30 mm through-hole. Add six Ø7 mm bolt holes on a Ø80 mm pitch circle. Create a 2 mm-wide annular sealing groove on the underside between Ø62 mm and Ø70 mm, 1.5 mm deep. All features must remain non-intersecting except for intentional bores and grooves.

### M09 — Machinable vise jaw
Model a 120 × 25 × 35 mm vise jaw. Cut two Ø10 mm counterbored mounting holes through the 35 mm height, with Ø16 mm counterbores 5 mm deep, spaced 80 mm apart. Add six vertical serration grooves on the clamping face, 2 mm pitch and 1 mm depth, with 60° V profiles. Keep the mounting holes fully enclosed by the jaw's material except where they open onto their intended faces.

### M10 — Flanged reducer
Create a concentric hollow reducer from Ø60 mm OD/Ø48 mm ID at the large end to Ø36 mm OD/Ø28 mm ID at the small end, with 70 mm overall length and a 50 mm-long conical transition between 10 mm straight end lands. Add 10 mm-thick end flanges: Ø90 mm at the large end and Ø60 mm at the small end, each with four Ø8 mm holes on respective Ø72 mm and Ø46 mm pitch circles. The internal fluid passage must transition smoothly without a solid plug.

### M11 — Hydraulic cylinder barrel end cap
Create an end cap for a nominal Ø50 mm hydraulic cylinder bore. The cap has an outer flange Ø80 mm × 10 mm thick, a cylindrical register Ø50 mm × 8 mm long, and a central rod opening Ø20 mm through. Add four Ø8.5 mm bolt holes on an Ø64 mm pitch circle. Add a concentric seal groove on the register face, 3 mm wide and 2 mm deep, maintaining clear material around the rod opening.

### M12 — Ribbed motor mounting plate
Create a 140 × 100 × 8 mm plate with a centred raised motor register Ø70 mm × 5 mm high and a Ø35 mm central clearance hole. Add four Ø9 mm mounting holes on a 105 × 70 mm rectangular pattern. Reinforce the underside with four ribs 6 mm thick and 18 mm tall, arranged as two orthogonal pairs without blocking the mounting holes. Fuse ribs and plate into one solid.

### M13 — Two-piece shaft coupling
Create a coupling assembly with two separate hubs, each Ø40 mm OD and 25 mm long, with a Ø12 mm shaft bore and a 4 mm-wide × 2 mm-deep keyway. Join the hubs through a 10 mm-thick flexible-style centre disc Ø55 mm with six equally spaced Ø6 mm holes on a Ø42 mm pitch circle. Keep the two hubs coaxial with a 2 mm axial gap to the centre disc on each side; preserve distinct components for assembly inspection.

### M14 — Four-hole flanged bearing sleeve
Create a bearing sleeve with Ø50 mm OD, Ø30 mm bore, and 40 mm body length. Add an integral mounting flange Ø90 mm × 8 mm thick at one end. Cut four Ø9 mm holes on a Ø68 mm pitch circle through the flange. Add a 2 mm-deep retaining ring groove inside the bore, 6 mm from the non-flanged end, while keeping at least 2 mm wall thickness.

### M15 — Sheet-metal electrical enclosure
Model a simplified folded enclosure made from 2 mm-thick sheet geometry, external dimensions 180 × 120 × 80 mm, open at the front. Add four 15 mm-deep inward mounting returns at the front edges, each with Ø5 mm holes. Include a separate 2 mm-thick removable front cover with six matching holes. Keep enclosure body and cover separate and make their mating perimeter align without interference.

### M16 — Two-stage shaft with bearing seats and keyways
Create a 160 mm-long stepped shaft with sections Ø20 × 30 mm, Ø30 × 50 mm, Ø25 × 40 mm, and Ø16 × 40 mm. Add two bearing seats Ø25 mm, each 20 mm long, on the Ø25 section; add two 5 mm-wide × 2.5 mm-deep keyways on designated Ø30 and Ø25 seats, each 30 mm long. Include 1.5 mm shoulder fillets where space permits and 0.5 mm end chamfers. Keep all sections coaxial.

### M17 — T-slot fixture plate
Create a 200 × 150 × 16 mm fixture plate with four parallel T-slots along the 200 mm direction. Each slot has a 10 mm-wide opening and a 16 mm-wide undercut cavity 6 mm deep from the underside of the top skin, leaving a 4 mm top lip geometry as appropriate to the section. Space slot centre lines evenly with 32 mm spacing. Add four Ø8 mm mounting holes near the corners without breaking into the slots.

### M18 — Hollow Y-manifold
Create a hollow Y-manifold with one inlet branch OD 40 mm/ID 30 mm and two outlet branches OD 32 mm/ID 24 mm. Use smooth branch junctions and centreline angles of ±35° relative to the inlet, with 50 mm straight lengths from each branch junction to the open ends. Add end flanges 8 mm thick with two Ø6 mm holes on a Ø46 mm pitch circle for the inlet and two Ø5.5 mm holes on a Ø38 mm pitch circle for each outlet. Validate that all three passages connect internally.

### M19 — Pump impeller basic geometry
Create a centrifugal impeller with a Ø100 mm shroud envelope, Ø25 mm central hub bore, and 20 mm axial height. Add six backward-curved vanes between a 30 mm inner radius and a 48 mm outer radius, with vane thickness 3 mm and consistent spacing. Include a 6 mm-thick rear disc and a 4 mm-thick front shroud with an inlet opening Ø40 mm. This is a geometric prototype; do not claim hydraulic performance from shape alone.

### M20 — Toggle clamp linkage parts
Create a simplified toggle clamp as an assembly with a 120 × 40 × 8 mm base, a 50 × 30 × 8 mm upright support, two 8 mm-thick links of lengths 65 mm and 45 mm, and a 100 mm handle. Use Ø8 mm pivot holes and shoulder pins at all specified joints. Arrange the links in a near-straight toggle position with a 5° over-centre condition and keep separate components. Motion validation is required only if the application supports kinematic simulation.

### M21 — Threaded flange adapter (nominal threads)
Create an adapter with a Ø60 mm × 10 mm flange, a 35 mm-long cylindrical spigot Ø32 mm, and a centred Ø20 mm flow bore throughout. Add four Ø7 mm flange holes on a Ø45 mm pitch circle. On the spigot, reserve a 20 mm-long nominal external M32×2 thread zone; represent it with a cylindrical envelope if true helical threads are unsupported. Preserve a continuous flow passage.

### M22 — Dowel-located two-part housing
Create a base housing 100 × 70 × 18 mm and a separate cap 100 × 70 × 12 mm. Together they enclose a cylindrical cavity Ø40 mm along the 100 mm axis. Add four M8 nominal clearance holes (Ø9 mm) through the cap and matching threaded-hole pilot bores Ø6.8 mm in the base. Add two Ø6 mm dowel holes at diagonally opposite positions, aligned between the two halves. Export the two parts as separate solids and as an assembled STEP.

### M23 — Shaft support with oil groove
Create a bearing support block 80 × 60 × 45 mm with a horizontal Ø30 mm bearing bore through its 80 mm length. Add a 2 mm-wide annular oil groove in the bore, 15 mm from one side face, at 1 mm depth into the bore wall. Add four Ø10 mm base mounting holes on a 60 × 40 mm pattern. Include 4 mm external edge fillets without changing the bore diameter or breaking through the mounting-hole walls unintentionally.

### M24 — Cam disc with offset follower track
Create a Ø100 mm × 12 mm cam disc around a central Ø20 mm bore. Add an eccentric circular pocket of Ø30 mm, 4 mm deep, whose centre is offset 15 mm from the shaft axis. Add a raised follower boss Ø18 mm × 5 mm on the opposite side, positioned 25 mm from the shaft axis. Include a 4 mm keyway in the central bore. Treat this as a geometric cam test; no motion law is implied by the eccentric pocket alone.

### M25 — Small conveyor idler roller assembly
Create an idler roller assembly 250 mm overall width with a 200 mm-long roller shell Ø60 mm OD and 4 mm wall thickness. Fit end hubs Ø40 mm OD × 20 mm long into both ends, with Ø12 mm axle bores. Add a Ø12 mm axle passing through the assembly, with retaining shoulders Ø18 mm at the ends. Keep shell, two hubs and axle separate, coaxial, and correctly positioned; verify the roller shell is hollow.

### M26 — Gearbox mounting foot
Create a mounting foot 120 × 80 × 10 mm with a vertical pedestal 70 × 50 × 45 mm. Place two coaxial bearing bores Ø35 mm through the pedestal along its 70 mm width, one on each side wall, with the bore centre 28 mm above the base. Add four Ø11 mm mounting slots in the base, each 24 × 11 mm overall. Add two ribs 6 mm thick between the pedestal and base without intruding into the bearing bore.

### M27 — Split clamp collar
Create a split shaft collar with outer diameter 50 mm, axial width 20 mm, and central bore Ø25 mm. Cut a radial split 3 mm wide from the outside to the bore. Add two Ø6.5 mm clamp-bolt holes perpendicular to the split, spaced 32 mm apart, and counterbores Ø10 mm × 4 mm deep on one side. The split must fully interrupt the ring, and the two bolt holes must be aligned to allow a clamping fastener to pass through.

### M28 — Adjustable slotted link
Create a 180 mm-long flat link 25 mm wide and 8 mm thick. Add a Ø12 mm hole at each end with centres 20 mm from each end. Cut a central longitudinal slot 70 mm overall length and 8 mm width, centred along the link. Add shallow 1 mm-deep relief pockets 18 × 15 mm near both ends. Maintain a minimum 5 mm ligament between slot edges and the side boundaries.

### M29 — Compact pneumatic cylinder body and piston
Create a simplified pneumatic cylinder assembly with a barrel OD 40 mm, ID 32 mm, and 100 mm length; separate end caps 10 mm thick at both ends; a piston Ø31.5 mm × 12 mm; and a Ø10 mm piston rod 80 mm long. Add two side air ports Ø6 mm to the barrel near opposite ends, each intersecting the bore. Add cap tie-rod holes at four corners on a 30 × 30 mm square pattern. Keep parts separate and arrange a plausible extended configuration without claiming pressure-rated design.

### M30 — Circular indexing plate with detents
Create an indexing plate Ø150 mm × 12 mm, with a centred Ø25 mm bore and twelve Ø8 mm holes evenly spaced on an Ø110 mm pitch circle. Add a shallow annular recess Ø80–Ø100 mm, 2 mm deep, on the top face. Add a separate spring-plunger housing block 30 × 20 × 18 mm with a Ø8 mm plunger guide and two Ø5 mm mounting holes. Position the housing so the plunger axis points toward the pitch-circle detent holes; preserve separate bodies.

